about is actually the
edge of this picture.

196
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:29,580
I'm a ghost who lives out
his days in a photograph.

197
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:33,880
I can control the space of
any picture in which I appear.

198
00:10:34,260 --> 00:10:38,940
By using that camera, I trap a person's
spiritual energy within a photograph.

199
00:10:39,460 --> 00:10:40,680
That's my power.

200
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:43,532
The room you're in is inside the picture.

201
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:47,620
Damaging the photo means damaging
the spiritual energy too,

202
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:49,777
which won't end well for you.

203
00:10:49,860 --> 00:10:52,160
But that doesn't make a lick of sense!

204
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:54,717
How are we in the picture
if I'm looking right at it?

205
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:58,457
You're clearly not the brightest,
so I'll spill it out for you.

206
00:10:58,540 --> 00:11:02,177
After I kill these two fools,
I'll ensnare you and the brat?

207
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:03,672
and shred you to pieces!

208
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:07,800
J-Jusuke! Mr. Jotaro!

209
00:11:10,780 --> 00:11:12,180
Time to die!

210
00:11:13,940 --> 00:11:14,770
Bastard!

211
00:11:14,853 --> 00:11:16,366
Get us out of here right now!

212
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:19,097
Jotaro, why are you just standing around?

213
00:11:19,180 --> 00:11:23,121
Your Star Platinum is super powerful,
so hurry up and do something!

214
00:11:23,740 --> 00:11:26,637
Sorry, Josuke, but I'm gonna
have to throw in the towel.

215
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:27,550
Huh?

216
00:11:27,633 --> 00:11:30,517
Stopping that old-timers
attacks is downright impossible.

217
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:34,457
Every bit of damage we throw at him
will only come right back to us.

218
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:38,011
Star Platinum could stop time,
but there's really no point.

219
00:11:38,620 --> 00:11:40,380
It'd be a waste of energy.

220
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:42,040
I can't believe it.

221
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:43,460
What are you saying?

222
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:46,480
Have you completely lost your mind?

223
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:49,180
Die! Die! Die!

224
00:11:58,260 --> 00:12:01,100
Your heads have got
some good spin to them.

225
00:12:02,020 --> 00:12:03,480
Great, he's got a knife.

226
00:12:10,280 --> 00:12:11,480
It's not working!

227
00:12:11,760 --> 00:12:13,240
I can't touch it, Jotaro!

228
00:12:13,620 --> 00:12:15,796
I've given up on stopping the geezer.

229
00:12:17,340 --> 00:12:18,170
However...

230
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:26,041
If he's being honest, it can really
control any photograph he's in.

231
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:29,817
But maybe the best way to win is to take a

232
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:32,606
shot of him so he's in
the picture by himself.

233
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:35,240
What the...

234
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:43,877
You found a way to sidestep
my attack entirely! Dammit!

235
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:46,357
Why don't you give our
friend here a nice send-off

236
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:49,381
and make sure you add a
little bit of style to it?

237
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:53,614
It looks like you weren't so
big and bad after all fool!

238
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:04,857
I Underestimated you, but I
see you're seasoned fighters?

239
00:13:04,940 --> 00:13:09,617
You've got lots of experience battling
opponents with special abilities like my son,

240
00:13:09,700 --> 00:13:10,530
don't you?

241
00:13:10,613 --> 00:13:13,869
Remember the old farts a ghost
he can get out of the picture

242
00:13:22,220 --> 00:13:25,396
We need to make sure you
behave yourself and stay put.

243
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:29,197
There's something in this house
you really don't want us to find.

244
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:32,868
That's why you're attacking us
with so much fervor, isn't it?

245
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:43,980
Oh, I get it.

246
00:13:44,100 --> 00:13:47,657
If you fold that crusty old prune in
half, there's no way he can get out.

247
00:13:47,740 --> 00:13:49,328
Looks like we win this one.

248
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:52,038
Okuyasu and Koichi search this room.

249
00:13:52,180 --> 00:13:54,004
Josuke and I have got this one.

250
00:13:55,740 --> 00:13:58,460
I can't protect my son
if I'm trapped in here.

251
00:13:58,660 --> 00:13:59,857
What am I going to do?

252
00:13:59,940 --> 00:14:02,528
If it falls into their
hands, it's all over.

253
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:12,517
What could he be hiding
that's so important

254
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:14,897
he'd do all this to
keep us from finding it?

255
00:14:14,980 --> 00:14:18,157
I don't have the foggiest clue,
but I'm not going to sweat it.

256
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:22,320
If the old man turns white as a
sheet, we should be good. Help me!

257
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:23,680
I can't breathe!

258
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:26,120
It's torture in here!

259
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:28,080
Can't I have a bit of air?

260
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:32,057
Just poke a couple of holes in the
tape and let me catch my breath!

261
00:14:32,140 --> 00:14:32,970
What?

262
00:14:33,053 --> 00:14:34,737
You seriously can't breathe in there?

263
00:14:34,820 --> 00:14:36,557
He's pulling your leg, Koichi.

264
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:37,637
Don't fall for it.

265
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:40,197
He wants you to make an
opening so he can get away.

266
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:44,162
I know you don't trust me, but I
really am dying in here, I swear!

267
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:46,277
I don't know about this, Okuyasu.

268
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:49,777
I'm claustrophobic, so I sort of get
what the poor guy's going through.

269
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:51,637
Oh, quit your bitchin', geezer.

270
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:55,537
If you really need a breathing hole
that bad, I'm more than happy to help.

271
00:14:55,620 --> 00:14:57,377
Here, how's that working out for ya?

272
00:14:57,460 --> 00:14:59,220
I know it's a little tacky.

273
00:14:59,660 --> 00:15:01,117
What do you think you're doing?

274
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:06,460
Damn it, get me out of here,
you wretched little punk!

275
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:08,899
Sounds like you caught your breath.

276
00:15:09,260 --> 00:15:11,613
Those tacks ain't going nowhere, Gramps.

277
00:15:12,020 --> 00:15:12,980
Tax, you say?

278
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:15,800
That must mean you stuck me to the post.

279
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:19,480
What a red-letter day.

280
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:24,036
You idiots don't realize it, but
those tacks are my ticket out of here.

281
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:27,600
I couldn't have planned it better myself.

282
00:15:28,140 --> 00:15:30,380
Much obliged, suckers. So long!

283
00:15:36,220 --> 00:15:37,960
Hey, you pruney old bastard!

284
00:15:38,260 --> 00:15:40,097
What the hell was that sound just now?

285
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:41,121
What did you do?

286
00:15:43,140 --> 00:15:44,477
Open your mouth, dammit!

287
00:15:44,560 --> 00:15:45,557
I'm talking to you!

288
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:46,917
I think we might have messed up!

289
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,529
What if he really used
the tacks to escape?

290
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,120
Mr. Jojuro!

291
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:52,913
Kira's father got away!

292
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:55,877
This mess is only happening because of me!

293
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:59,019
I stuck some tacks in it
and he did something weird!

294
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:05,694
You've been duped, my blockhead friend!

295
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:08,194
That was a battle of wits and you lost!

296
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:11,000
You mean he was faking?

297
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:16,800
There's no way!

298
00:16:17,140 --> 00:16:20,297
I mean, this is the bow and
arrow, but why is it here?

299
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:21,777
I just don't understand.

300
00:16:21,860 --> 00:16:24,154
We already retrieved them from Otoishi.

301
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:27,557
I thought the Speedwagon
Foundation was guarding them.

302
00:16:27,640 --> 00:16:28,600
What's going on?

303
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:30,320
Is this another set?

304
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:32,100
Hey, watch out!

305
00:16:32,380 --> 00:16:33,909
Kira's father has escaped!

306
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:37,180
Damn it!

307
00:16:37,380 --> 00:16:40,397
This is the very arrow that
brought forth Deadly Queen!

308
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:42,715
Whoever wields it holds all the power!

309
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:44,980
I'll never let you take it from me!

310
00:16:57,980 --> 00:16:59,480
Use Reverb, Koichi!

311
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:01,837
Sick Act 1 on him! I can't!

312
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:03,417
He's already too far away!

313
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:04,440
Freaking great!

314
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:08,237
At least now we know what Kira's father
was trying to stop us from finding!

315
00:17:08,320 --> 00:17:10,438
He was hiding another bow and arrow!

316
00:17:12,580 --> 00:17:13,410
Dammit!

317
00:17:13,493 --> 00:17:14,540
It's all my fault!

318
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:15,760
No, Okuyasu.

319
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:17,740
He simply outsmarted us.

320
00:17:17,980 --> 00:17:20,340
That geezer's definitely Kira's father.

321
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:21,952
There's no mistaking it.

322
00:17:22,100 --> 00:17:24,688
They're gonna fight to
survive at all costs.

323
00:17:24,780 --> 00:17:28,251
Their unrelenting resolve is
what's getting the best of us.

324
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:33,157
As long as those chumps don't
get this arrow, we'll be fine.

325
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:37,137
And in the meantime, I'll use it to
make even more enemies for them to face.

326
00:17:37,220 --> 00:17:38,480
The bow and arrow.

327
00:17:38,820 --> 00:17:39,740
So it's true.

328
00:17:40,020 --> 00:17:42,902
I had a feeling there
might be more than one set.

329
00:17:43,320 --> 00:17:46,057
That would explain how Dio
and his henchmen were able to

330
00:17:46,140 --> 00:17:49,611
pull together such a large
group of stand users so quickly.

331
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:52,077
They built an army of minions across the

332
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:54,807
globe using multiple
sets of bows and arrows.

333
00:17:56,740 --> 00:18:00,560
Kira's father probably obtained
this set from Inyaba the Witch.

334
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:04,317
And we already know Okuyasu's
brother Keicho came into

335
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:08,047
possession of one at some point
before they arrived in Morioh.

336
00:18:09,140 --> 00:18:12,258
Stand users really do seem
to be drawn to each other.

337
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:17,300
Oh Yoshikage, where are you?

338
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:21,537
Even as a little boy, you couldn't
repress your urges to kill women.

339
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:25,377
But if that's what makes you happy,
I'll support and protect you.

340
00:18:25,460 --> 00:18:27,160
That's my duty as a parent.

341
00:18:30,540 --> 00:18:35,060
So, as you're my one and only
son, I'll do all I can for you.

342
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:42,237
I can't say I've ever seen
this side of you before.

343
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:44,617
I mean, since when do you know
your way around a kitchen?

344
00:18:44,700 --> 00:18:46,759
It's not some kind of prank, is it?

345
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:49,657
There's two plates here,
so I assume one's mine.

346
00:18:49,740 --> 00:18:53,197
You can't possibly think I'd eat
something you slopped together.

347
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:54,260
That's insane.

348
00:18:57,820 --> 00:18:58,650
Seriously?

349
00:18:58,860 --> 00:19:01,757
Do you really think now is the
best time to cut your nails?

350
00:19:01,840 --> 00:19:04,437
Besides, you cut them
last night, didn't you?

351
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:06,440
They sure grow fast.

352
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:14,860
Holy shit!

353
00:19:15,140 --> 00:19:16,728
This is actually delicious!

354
00:19:35,580 --> 00:19:37,177
To be

355
00:19:37,260 --> 00:19:44,260
continued...

356
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:52,505
I'm going to have to tell
you to leave it open!

357
00:19:54,120 --> 00:19:56,257
Oh my goodness, what's
the matter, sweetie?

358
00:19:56,340 --> 00:19:58,281
Why are you getting so worked up?

359
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:09,426
I guess cats aren't the
biggest fans of water.

360
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:10,580
My apologies.

361
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,294
I wasn't thinking and acted carelessly.

362
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:15,286
Sorry, it won't happen again.

363
00:20:18,460 --> 00:20:21,257
There's definitely something
strange going on with him.

364
00:20:21,340 --> 00:20:25,177
First he starts cooking for
me out of the blue and now

365
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:27,717
he's using an actual blade
instead of his electric razor.

366
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:30,417
Blades always give him razor burn.

367
00:20:30,500 --> 00:20:35,137
Listen, pal, you still haven't
paid last month's rent.

368
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:36,050
You cheapskate.

369
00:20:36,133 --> 00:20:37,457
Now you owe for this month.

370
00:20:37,540 --> 00:20:38,370
So?

371
00:20:38,453 --> 00:20:40,681
We'll fork over the yen,
not leave until I'm paid!

372
00:20:41,840 --> 00:20:42,670
Rent?

373
00:20:44,360 --> 00:20:45,500
You are the man.

374
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:49,097
Go and get the money from the
safe before he kicks us out.

375
00:20:49,180 --> 00:20:50,100
Ride the safe.

376
00:20:50,780 --> 00:20:51,960
Get a move on.

377
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:53,417
What are you waiting for?

378
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:54,971
You have the combination.

379
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:00,498
What are you doing?

380
00:21:00,620 --> 00:21:01,620
Get back up here!

381
00:21:02,980 --> 00:21:05,637
Thank you for taking the
time to drop by this morning.

382
00:21:05,720 --> 00:21:08,497
But I appear to be running a
bit short on cash at the moment.

383
00:21:08,580 --> 00:21:09,992
I'm sure you understand.

384
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:11,270
Huh?

385
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:13,897
Oh, that hair gel must be
seeping into your noggin?

386
00:21:13,980 --> 00:21:15,597
I should have known you young deadbeats!

387
00:21:15,680 --> 00:21:17,577
Wouldn't be able to
afford my gorgeous home.

388
00:21:17,660 --> 00:21:20,317
That's what I get for doing
business with schmucks!

389
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:22,500
Learn to live within your means.

390
00:21:23,980 --> 00:21:24,937
You'll get your money!

391
00:21:25,020 --> 00:21:27,337
No, I think you misunderstood me earlier.

392
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:29,337
I said I was short on cash.

393
00:21:29,420 --> 00:21:32,600
but I meant that I only
had a little over $500,000.

394
00:21:34,840 --> 00:21:37,157
I'll only be able to pay for this month,

395
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:40,157
last month, and for the next
couple of months in advance.

396
00:21:40,240 --> 00:21:41,769
Will that suffice for now?

397
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:43,640
Yes, that'll do nicely.

398
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:45,520
Thanks so much.

399
00:21:45,620 --> 00:21:46,561
Have a good one.

400
00:21:47,280 --> 00:21:48,640
Until next time.

401
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:51,880
What was that?

402
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:56,936
I don't know how, but you
must have stolen that money.

403
00:21:57,020 --> 00:21:59,337
There's no point trying
to say that you didn't.

404
00:21:59,420 --> 00:22:02,302
You stole it from the
landlord's bag, didn't you?

405
00:22:03,520 --> 00:22:05,637
If anyone else was in this situation,

406
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:09,077
they'd be horrified that their
partner could do such a thing.

407
00:22:09,160 --> 00:22:10,200
But his gusto.

408
00:22:10,600 --> 00:22:13,835
The way he stole the money
and lied about it so easily.

409
00:22:14,100 --> 00:22:18,937
I've been with him for so many years, but
he's never made me feel like this before.

410
00:22:19,020 --> 00:22:20,300
It's exhilarating!

411
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:26,080
It's like I'm falling in love
with him for the first time.

412
00:22:51,540 --> 00:22:53,917
Anytime I need to see your
face, it has closed my eyes.

413
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:56,177
And I am taking two bits
for your crystal mind!

414
00:22:56,260 --> 00:22:58,977
A magenta feeling, take a
shelter in the face of my spine.

415
00:22:59,060 --> 00:23:00,357
Like a Chaka cherry cola.

416
00:23:00,440 --> 00:23:01,777
I don't need to try to explain?

417
00:23:01,860 --> 00:23:02,957
I just hold on tight.

418
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:04,037
And if it happens again?

419
00:23:04,120 --> 00:23:05,277
I'ma move so slightly.

420
00:23:05,360 --> 00:23:06,417
To the arms and the lips.

421
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:07,330
And the face.

422
00:23:07,413 --> 00:23:08,243
Of the humic.

423
00:23:08,326 --> 00:23:09,156
And the ball.

424
00:23:09,239 --> 00:23:10,069
That I need to.

425
00:23:10,152 --> 00:23:10,982
I want to.

426
00:23:11,065 --> 00:23:11,895
Come and stand.

427
00:23:11,978 --> 00:23:12,808
A little bit closer.

428
00:23:12,891 --> 00:23:13,721
Breathe in.

429
00:23:13,804 --> 00:23:14,634
And get a bit higher.

430
00:23:14,717 --> 00:23:16,077
You'll never know. What hit you.

431
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:18,457
When I get to you.

432
00:23:18,540 --> 00:23:20,297
Oh I want you.

433
00:23:20,380 --> 00:23:21,210
I don't know.

434
00:23:21,293 --> 00:23:22,717
If I need you.

435
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:24,897
Oh I want you.

436
00:23:24,980 --> 00:23:25,980
If I need help.

437
00:23:27,460 --> 00:23:31,840
Ooh, I want you, I don't
know if I need you.

438
00:23:32,820 --> 00:23:34,980
Ooh, I'm trying to find you.
